{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi98wucf8uVij5gGmXSA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H5pfvxUC8yP66aqDR1iMbt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-073322__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1 | cut -c1-30; rm -rf .tmp node_modules; cd ..; sed -i 's/two small marked changes/three small marked changes/; s/Two changes, both marked/Three changes, all marked/' exit-interview.json; python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\nd['sourceInformation']['animation']=d['sourceInformation']['animation'].replace('keeper dives','keeper dives and bicycle kicks (with a new whole-body tilt added to the engine rig)')\nd['engineFeedback'][4]=\"Three changes, all marked `// EF:` and recorded in engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md: E.Dialog's `voice` may be a function (babble per speaker); E.Humanoid takes a `kit` option (hoops, stripes, halves, sash, shirt number); and E.Humanoid.update takes `tilt: { axis, angle, lift }`, a whole-body tilt about the hips so keeper dives, diving headers and bicycle kicks lean for real.\"\nd['engineFeedback'][3]=\"Lateral whole-body motion: the rig could only lie along its facing, roll forward or hop, so I added a tilt state to the engine myself. Working out which engine pieces are private (audio buses and the noise buffer) for the crowd engine was the other friction.\"\nd['engineFeedback'][5]=\"A `game.go(scene, data, { fade: 0 })` default for headless games so tests need not know about the fade, and a documented way to reach the audio context for custom crowd sound.\"\njson.dump(d,open('exit-interview.json','w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)\nEOF\ncd EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1 | cut -c1-30; python3 -I -c \"impo