{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi9Ycp5Zcwba24Z2ifg6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I captured a live goalkeeper dive in actual play: a penalty came in, the keeper dived (the dive event fired) and parried it. The \"PARRIED!\" notice is on screen and the keeper's body is horizontal mid-dive.\n\nThat is a real in-match capture, not a frozen frame. It is a still image, not video, so the motion itself is still covered only by the headless tilt checks plus this frame. I did not do a live capture of a bicycle kick.\n\nThe goal replay was likewise checked as a live capture (turned camera, REPLAY badge, letterbox, SKIP), not just a headless run.\n\nThe previous full suite run on this same build (107 checks) and the AI Hub harness runs on this file still stand. Usage stays \"unknown\" because I have no token or cost figures for this session, and the task allows \"unknown\" for anything I cannot confirm.\n\nThe game (`EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322.html`) and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:33:22\n- **Source:** European football (an over-the-top arcade take on it)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (Europhoria Football, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort). TASK.md won where they disagreed, so file and folder names use claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports, 5-a-side football with a five-round Cup Run, 1–4 local players and online versus. A TV broadcast camera, side-on and raised 40°, with Classic (55°) and Aerial (78°) options. Goal replays cut between three turned angles.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with three small marked changes, plain JavaScript built into one HTML file, AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0 unmodified, Playwright 1.63.0 for checks. No other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-art look