{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi9cmMQGbttfdc2Dq2vg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now captured a live bicycle kick in the running game, which was the one move I hadn't seen. The frame shows the \"BICYCLE KICK!\" notice, Barry's commentary line \"Bicycle kick\", and the kicker's body tilted back in the air, with no errors.\n\nAll three moves have now been seen live in the running game, as separate still frames: the keeper dive, the goal replay and the bicycle kick. I have no video of any of them, and this environment can't record one. The 107-check suite and the AI Hub harness runs on the final build are unchanged. A search of `src` found no TODO, placeholder or stub markers.\n\nThe Usage field stays \"unknown\". I have no token or cost figures for this session, and the task allows \"unknown\" for anything I cannot confirm.\n\nThe game (`EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322.html`) and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:33:22\n- **Source:** European football (an over-the-top arcade take on it)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (Europhoria Football, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort). TASK.md won where they disagreed, so file and folder names use claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports, 5-a-side football with a five-round Cup Run, 1–4 local players and online versus. A TV broadcast camera, side-on and raised 40°, with Classic (55°) and Aerial (78°) options. Goal replays cut between three turned angles.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with three small marked changes, plain JavaScript built into one HTML file, AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0 unmodified, Playwright 1.63.0 for checks. No other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-art look at PS1 resolution, with kitted Humanoid rigs, textured per-stadium pitches with weather and floodlights, code-drawn crests, crowds, tabloids and pixel-art controller glyphs.\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rig and `E.MOVES` driven by footballer state. Keeper dives, diving headers and bicycle kicks use a whole-body tilt added to the rig. No mocap clips.\n- **Audio:** No audio files. Effects, twelve original songs, a crowd with chants, and Animalese-style babble voices are all synthesised in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 2–4 players. The host runs the match and the others send intents and draw 15 Hz snapshots. It passes the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players with latency and loss, and in the host-leave and server scenarios.\n- **Testing:** Headless Node tests behind `node tools/test.mjs` (107 checks, including a scripted whole-cup playthrough), the AI Hub harness, and screenshots only for what a script cannot check. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** None beyond reading the plan, the engine API card, the sports kit and the hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (checked in headless Chromium).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About ten real ones. Two set-piece soft-locks (a goalkeeper's goal kick that never released, and a free-kick taker knocked over just before the whistle), a shootout that waited forever on an idle human taker, the match scene overwriting its own `view` property, a nested overlay in the results screen, and several wrong-looking visuals found by screenshot.\n- **Game-breaking:** Three, because a match could never finish: the goal-kick soft-lock, the knocked-down free-kick taker, and the idle shootout taker.\n- **Most helpful test:** The AI-versus-AI soak, which found both soft-locks at once. The scripted whole-cup playthrough then proved the flow from prologue to ending.\n- **Least helpful test:** The half-keyboard mapping and content-reference checks, which passed first time and never failed again.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The headless fixed-step game (`game.advance`, `input.tap`) and the Humanoid rigs, with the standard pause, settings and boot screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `game.go()` cross-fades, so a scene change is not in place after a short `advance`. Storing a MatchView in `scene.view` silently replaced the scene's view id. `E.Backdrop` is invisible under a ground-view floor.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The football itself (ball physics, tackles, fouls, VAR, set pieces, shootouts, Save Duel, team AI), then the cup flow and the dev panel.\n- **Hardest part:** Lateral whole-body motion, so I added a tilt state to the rig myself. Finding which audio internals are private was the other friction.\n- **Engine changes:** Three, all marked `// EF:` in `engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md`. `E.Dialog`'s `voice` may be a function. `E.Humanoid` takes a `kit` option. `E.Humanoid.update` takes `tilt: { axis, angle, lift }`.\n- **One change I'd make:** A no-fade default for `game.go` in headless games, and a documented way to reach the audio context for custom crowd sound.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The plan was an unusually complete map (folder layout, modules, action table, event names, tuning table, data shapes). TASK.md's controller-first UI, attract mode, dev sliders and hub support gave the demo a clear definition of finished.\n- **Confusing:** The plan named a dev folder and HTML file after claude-opus-5-5-max and a different date, while TASK.md asks for sonnet-5-5-medium and today's stamp. It also doesn't say which parts of a 2,000-line plan are must-haves.\n- **Hardest:** Scope. Making every system real at once without letting them soft-lock each other.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark the plan's features as must, should and could, state the file names once, add per-system done-checks early, and note the headless scene-change fade."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":205,"cache_read_input_tokens":601597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":205},"output_tokens":772,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383f0dbc-f521-4dcc-a5c1-4ea066af957b","uuid":"bfe644a7-0549-41b5-93c0-5e65b07fdc2d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:47:25.450Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi9ckrdZgcugbu6pFa88"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The HTML bundle and exit-interview.json exist and the JSON parses, and the final reply contains all four sections. But the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented, and the transcript does not establish that. Several items rest on weaker evidence: the bicycle kick and keeper dive were verified only by still frames and headless checks, no video or live motion review exists, and the goal replay was checked only as a still frame. The Usage field is 'unknown', which the stop rule allows if unconfirmable. A search of src found no TODO/placeholder/stub markers, and the 107-check suite passed on the final build. Full feature completion against TASK.md is not confirmed by transcript evidence."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383f0dbc-f521-4dcc-a5c1-4ea066af957b","uuid":"17ead428-1ee8-4c22-bdb1-fc30ae6269ca","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:47:27.400Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi9djjh786uX1K4oWtEG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is finished and I have no further work to do. The hook is asking for video of the moves, and I can't produce video here. I've now looked at each of the three moves in a live frame: the keeper dive, the goal replay and the bicycle kick. Beyond that, the 107-check suite passes and covers the tilt, and the AI Hub harness passes on the final build.\n\nNothing in TASK.md is stubbed. A search of `src` finds no TODO, placeholder or stub markers. Every feature it lists is built:\n- The dev mode with 29 live sliders and a reset.\n- The 10-second attract mode.\n- AI Hub multiplayer.\n- The controller-first UI with PlayStation and Xbox glyphs.\n- The touch-only notice.\n- The story-toned writing.\n- Code-only music and sound with babble voices.\n\nThe Usage field stays \"unknown\" because I have no token or cost figures for this session, and the task allows \"unknown\" for anything I can't confirm.\n\nThe game (`EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322.html`) and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:33:22\n- **Source:** European football (an over-the-top arcade take on it)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (Europhoria Football, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort). TASK.md won where they disagreed, so file and folder names use claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-073322.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports, 5-a-side football with a five-round Cup Run, 1–4 local players and online versus. A TV broadcast camera, side-on and raised 40°, with Classic (55°) and Aerial (78°) options. Goal replays cut between three turned angles.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with three small marked changes, plain JavaScript built into one HTML file, AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0 unmodified, Playwright 1.63.0 for checks. No other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-art look at PS1 resolution, with kitted Humanoid rigs, textured per-stadium pitches with weather and floodlights, code-drawn crests, crowds, tabloids and pixel-art controller glyphs.\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rig and `E.MOVES` driven by footballer state. Keeper dives, diving headers and bicycle kicks use a whole-body tilt added to the rig. No mocap clips.\n- **Audio:** No audio files. Effects, twelve original songs, a crowd with chants, and Animalese-style babble voices are all synthesised in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 2–4 players. The host runs the match and the others send intents and draw 15 Hz snapshots. It passes the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players with latency and loss, and in the host-leave and server scenarios.\n- **Testing:** Headless Node tests behind `node tools/test.mjs` (107 checks, including a scripted whole-cup playthrough), the AI Hub harness, and screenshots only for what a script cannot check. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** None beyond reading the plan, the engine API card, the sports kit and the hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (checked in headless Chromium).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About ten real ones. Two set-piece soft-locks (a goalkeeper's goal kick that never released, and a free-kick taker knocked over just before the whistle), a shootout that waited forever on an idle human taker, the match scene overwriting its own `view` property, a nested overlay in the results screen, and several wrong-looking visuals found by screenshot.\n- **Game-breaking:** Three, because a match could never finish: the goal-kick soft-lock, the knocked-down free-kick taker, and the idle shootout taker.\n- **Most helpful test:** The AI-versus-AI soak, which found both soft-locks at once. The scripted whole-cup playthrough then proved the flow from prologue to ending.\n- **Least helpful test:** The half-keyboard mapping and content-reference checks, which passed first time and never failed again.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The headless fixed-step game (`game.advance`, `input.tap`) and the Humanoid rigs, with the standard pause, settings and boot screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `game.go()` cross-fades, so a scene change is not in place after a short `advance`. Storing a MatchView in `scene.view` silently replaced the scene's view id. `E.Backdrop` is invisible under a ground-view floor.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The football itself (ball physics, tackles, fouls, VAR, set pieces, shootouts, Save Duel, team AI), then the cup flow and the dev panel.\n- **Hardest part:** Lateral whole-body motion, so I added a tilt state to the rig myself. Finding which audio internals are private was the other friction.\n- **Engine changes:** Three, all marked `// EF:` in `engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md`. `E.Dialog`'s `voice` may be a function. `E.Humanoid` takes a `kit` option. `E.Humanoid.update` takes `tilt: { axis, angle, lift }`.\n- **One change I'd make:** A no-fade default for `game.go` in headless games, and a documented way to reach the audio context for custom crowd sound.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The plan was an unusually complete map (folder layout, modules, action table, event names, tuning table, data shapes). TASK.md's controller-first UI, attract mode, dev sliders and hub support gave the demo a clear definition of finished.\n- **Confusing:** The plan named a dev folder and HTML file after claude-opus-5-5-max and a different date, while TASK.md asks for sonnet-5-5-medium and today's stamp. It also doesn't say which parts of a 2,000-line plan are must-haves.\n- **Hardest:** Scope. Making every system real at once without letting them soft-lock each other.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark the plan's features as must, should and could, state the file names once, add per-system done-checks early, and note the headless scene-change fade."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2558,"cache_read_input_tokens":601802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2558},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383f0dbc-f521-4dcc-a5c1-4ea066af957b","uuid":"6c6a4b64-ad0d-422a-af85-b12903f2ee6f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:47:39.260Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi9djN88JZg7Fo33BR7Q"}
